    trap: 'The scheme model is \'Slope of l = ½; lines drawn parallel to l and touching p(x) at x ≈ 2·2 and x ≈ 6·8\' on Scale 15D (0, 4, 6, 8, 15). The classic miss is treating it like p(x) = l(x) and reading off where the two graphs CROSS, which is the wrong idea entirely; the scheme also explicitly caps as Low Partial Credit (4/15) anyone who \'draws a horizontal line at y = ½\' (confusing the slope value ½ with a y-value) or who \'draws two parallel tangents to p(x) that are not parallel to l(x)\'. Even drawing both tangents correctly but never reading the x-values off the diagram caps you at High Partial Credit (\'Two tangents drawn correctly\') — the cue says estimate these two values of x, so the read-off is the marked final step.',
