    subjectId: 'business', subjectLabel: 'Business', level: 'ordinary',
    questionRef: '2025 OL · Section 1 Q4 · Finance (Break-Even)',
    stem: 'Complete the break-even chart above by writing the correct label — Total Revenue (TR), Total Cost (TC), Fixed Cost (FC) or Break-Even Point (BEP) — beside each of A, B, C and D.',
    commandWord: 'Complete',
    demand: 'Read the lines off the chart, not the textbook. Match each label to what the line/point on this chart actually does: the flat horizontal line (box D) is Fixed Cost; the steepest line rising from the origin (box B) is Total Revenue; the line starting at the fixed-cost level and rising less steeply (box C) is Total Cost; and the point where TR crosses TC (box A) is the Break-Even Point. \'Complete\' is marked label-by-label, so every box scores on its own.',
    trap: 'The classic swap is reading the two upward-sloping lines the wrong way round — labelling B as Total Cost and C as Total Revenue. Total Revenue starts at €0 (zero output, zero sales) and is the steeper line, while Total Cost starts up at the Fixed-Cost value; getting this pair backwards puts the Break-Even Point in the wrong place too. The scheme marks A, B, C, D separately (3 + 3 + 2 + 2), so each mislabelled line is its own lost mark.',
    source: 'SEC LC Business 2025 OL marking scheme, Section 1 Q4: A Break-Even Point (BEP), B Total Revenue (TR), C Total Cost (TC), D Fixed Cost (FC); 10m split 3 + 3 + 2 + 2',
