    demand: '"Discuss" here demands a two-sided economic argument, not a list of points. The scheme awards developed economic statements on BOTH sides: at least one advantage (e.g. low collection cost / evasion is harder / acts as a built-in stabiliser / less distortionary than income tax) AND at least one disadvantage (e.g. it is regressive — lower-income groups spend a greater proportion of income on the taxed goods — or it raises inflation / cost of living). Each correct point must be named and then explained with economic reasoning to earn full marks.',
    trap: 'The award is "2 @ 6" (12 marks) and the scheme states you "Must have a MINIMUM of ONE advantage / disadvantage." A candidate who reads "Discuss" as "list" and writes only advantages (or only disadvantages) — even two well-explained ones on one side — is capped at one side\'s marks and cannot reach the full 12; both an advantage and a disadvantage must appear. Naming a point without the economic explanation also forfeits half the marks on that point.',
