    demand: 'Read the two coordinates straight off the demand curve (€4 at Q = 8, then €5 at Q = 4), substitute into the elasticity formula the scheme uses — (ΔQ/ΔP) × ((P₁+P₂)/(Q₁+Q₂)) = (−4/+1) × (9/12) — and report the answer as −3. The marks reward correct points read off the graph PLUS the worked substitution that lands on −3, not a bare number.',
    trap: 'PED for a normal good is negative — the scheme\'s worked line ends \'(8 + 4) = −3\', keeping the minus sign. Drop the sign and write \'3\', or invert ΔQ and ΔP, and you forfeit the calculation marks: the diagram-read figures and the signed result must both be shown, so a stray positive answer or unshown workings is not awarded full credit.',
