    subjectId: 'agricultural-science', subjectLabel: 'Agricultural Science', level: 'higher',
    questionRef: '2024 HL · Q17(c)(ii)',
    stem: 'A student determined the percentage organic matter of two 90 g soil samples. The peat sample had a loss in mass of 55.2 g on ignition. Calculate A the % soil organic matter in the peat sample.',
    commandWord: 'Calculate',
    demand: 'Calculate = show the worked computation AND land the correct value. Here %OM = loss in mass / sample mass × 100 = 55.2 / 90 × 100 = 61.3%. The loss in mass on ignition (55.2 g) IS the organic matter burnt off, and the denominator is the 90 g starting sample - so the answer must be a percentage, expressed with the % sign.',
    trap: 'The scheme is split-mark: \'If a candidate gives 61.3 or 61 without showing calculation, award 6m. If the candidate gives the correct formula without correct answer, award 3m.\' So writing the formula 55.2/90 × 100 but botching the arithmetic caps you at HALF marks (3 of 6). Dividing by the wrong base (e.g. by 55.2, or treating the loss as already a %) gives a wrong value and forfeits the 3 result-marks.',
