    trap: 'The scheme\'s \'Subject Knowledge\' band caps you in the Low zone for mere recall with \'a limited level of critical thinking to analyse and evaluate\' — so a biography of Picasso or a narrated timeline with no analysis stalls in the bottom band. And \'Relevant Examples\' awards 10 marks specifically for named artists and named artworks: write about \'Cubism\' in the abstract with no specific named work to point at and that whole 10 marks collapses, dragging the essay down regardless of fluent writing.',
    source: 'LC Art (Visual Studies) 2025 HL marking scheme, Section B, Q12 ("Discuss the development of one of the following: Fauvism, Expressionism, Cubism, Bauhaus, Surrealism.")',
