    questionRef: '2024 HL · Q10(a)(i)',
    stem: 'The diagram below shows the scheduling network for manufacturing a car. Each edge is an activity with its duration in weeks in brackets, from A(3) to N(4); dashed unlabelled edges are not real activities but show the order in which activities must happen. Calculate the early time and the late time for each event. Complete the diagram below by writing the early time (upper box) and late time (lower box) at the node representing each event.',
