    trap: 'The completed diagram IS the answer — 20 marks scaled [0/8/14/17]. One systemic error (taking the shortest route on the forward pass, or copying early times into the late-time boxes instead of working backwards from the 21-week sink) drops the award to 17; two drop it to 14; empty boxes earn nothing because there is no other working to credit.',
    source: 'LC Applied Mathematics 2024 Higher Level marking scheme, Q10(a)(i) (completed early/late-time diagram awarded 20 marks [0/8/14/17]; (ii) critical path "B, E, J, L, M" = 21 weeks, consistent with (iv): K at 5 weeks makes B, E, K, N = 21 a second critical path with "no effect on the time")',
    marks: 20,
    figure: { src: '/exam-figures/applied-maths/am-complete-early-late-times-hl.png', alt: 'Activity-on-edge project network for manufacturing a car: 14 labelled activity edges A(3) to N(4) with durations in weeks, three dashed dummy edges, and a source node (left) and sink node (right). Each event node is an empty box pair, the upper box for the early time and the lower box for the late time, to be completed.', source: 'SEC Leaving Certificate Applied Mathematics 2024 Higher Level, Q10(a) — © State Examinations Commission' },
