    questionRef: '2023 HL · Q7(b)(iii)',
    stem: 'A student wishes to be able to spell 2000 difficult words. The rate of the student\'s learning is modelled by the differential equation dN/dt = k(2000 − N), where N(t) is the number of these words the student can spell after t hours of learning, and N(0) = 250. Sketch the shape of a graph of N against t to show the model\'s prediction for the student\'s learning curve.',
