    demand: 'A sketch on the printed axes carrying the model\'s key features — your part (i) solution is N = 2000 − 1750e^(−kt), so the curve must start at (0, 250), rise steeply at first, then flatten as it approaches the saturation value N = 2000 without ever crossing it.',
    trap: '\'Sketch the shape\' means the FEATURES are the answer: the scheme\'s 5-mark drawing shows the intercept at 250 and the levelling-off toward the 2000 asymptote on the given axes (N to 2400, t to 30). A straight line, a curve starting at 0, or one that crosses 2000 contradicts the solved model and forfeits all 5 marks.',
    source: 'LC Applied Mathematics 2023 Higher Level marking scheme, Q7(b)(iii) (5-mark sketch: curve from (0, 250) flattening toward N = 2000; from (i) "N = 2000 − 1750e^(−kt)" and (ii) k = ln 3.5 ÷ 6 ≅ 0.209 hour⁻¹)',
    marks: 5,
    figure: { src: '/exam-figures/applied-maths/am-sketch-learning-curve-hl.png', alt: 'Printed blank graphing axes from 2023 HL Applied Maths Q7(b)(iii): gridded plane with vertical axis labelled N (words) marked 400 to 2400 and horizontal axis labelled t (hours) marked 5 to 30, for sketching the learning curve.', source: 'SEC Leaving Certificate Applied Mathematics 2023 Higher Level, Q7(b)(iii) — © State Examinations Commission' },
