    subjectId: 'applied-mathematics', subjectLabel: 'Applied Mathematics', level: 'higher',
    questionRef: '2024 HL · Q3(b)(ii)',
    stem: 'Two identical smooth spheres, A and B, each moving with speed u, collide obliquely. The line joining their centres at impact is along the i-axis, and before the collision each sphere\'s velocity makes an acute angle α with the line of centres. The coefficient of restitution between the spheres is e. A and B move perpendicularly to each other after the collision. Show that e = tan α.',
