    demand: 'Derive the GIVEN result forwards: take the after-impact velocities from part (i) — A has −eu cos α·i + u sin α·j and B has eu cos α·i + u sin α·j (from conservation of momentum and Newton\'s experimental law) — impose perpendicularity as a zero dot product, −e²u²cos²α + u²sin²α = 0, and reduce it to tan²α/e² = 1, finishing at exactly e = tan α.',
    trap: 'Using the target as an input: substituting e = tan α into the velocities to "check" they are perpendicular is the derivation backwards and earns nothing — the scheme\'s single 5-mark award is for reaching "tan²α/e² = 1 so e = tan α as required", i.e. the perpendicularity condition must be the starting equation and e = tan α the conclusion.',
