    marks: 5,
    figure: { src: '/exam-figures/applied-maths/am-show-that-e-tan-alpha-hl.png', alt: 'Diagram: two identical smooth spheres A and B touching at the point of impact, the line of centres along the horizontal i-axis. Each sphere approaches with speed u; sphere A\'s velocity makes acute angle alpha above the positive i-direction and sphere B\'s makes angle alpha above the negative i-direction. A j-axis points perpendicular to the line of centres, shown by an i/j axis legend top-right.', source: 'SEC Leaving Certificate Applied Mathematics 2024 Higher Level, Q3(b) — © State Examinations Commission' },
