    trap: 'Dropping the constant of integration or never applying v = 4 at s = 0. The scheme\'s three 5-mark awards are: ln(v² + 392); = −s/20 + c; and c = ln 408 with the explicit v = √(408e^(−s/20) − 392). A general solution with c left unsolved loses the closing 5 marks — and sinks part (v), where v = 0 in YOUR expression must give the greatest height s = 20 ln(408/392) = 0.8 m.',
    source: 'LC Applied Mathematics 2025 HL marking scheme, Q2(iv) ("v = 4 when s = 0 so c = ln 408 … v = √(408e^(−s/20) − 392)")',
