    questionRef: '2024 HL · Q8(a)(ii)',
    stem: 'A company director designs a four-year business plan as a network: the edges represent promotion strategies, each with an estimated profit or loss (in €1000s, some negative), and the nodes represent the possible states of the plan. In part (i) you used Bellman\'s Principle of Optimality to find the plan that maximises profit. State one difference between Bellman\'s Principle of Optimality and Dijkstra\'s algorithm.',
