    subjectId: 'applied-mathematics', subjectLabel: 'Applied Mathematics', level: 'ordinary',
    questionRef: '2023 OL · Q10(v)',
    stem: 'An accounting company processes an account using a scheduling network with activities A to L (durations in minutes shown in brackets). From earlier parts, the critical path is B→D→J→K and the minimum completion time is 359 minutes. Exactly one hour after the processing of an account has begun, a supervisor checks the work. State which activity (or activities) must be happening at this time. Justify your answer.',
