    demand: 'Give a developed point about the presentation itself, with a concrete reference to the source: name a strength of the layout (e.g. the table sets the three countries side by side so the figures — like 4.9m, 8.9m, 15.8m people in need — are easy to compare at a glance, and the pictures add context) rather than commenting on the topic of hunger.',
    trap: 'Answering about hunger or the countries instead of how the data is presented misses the cue, and a bare one-liner (\'it\'s clear\') with no developed reason caps at the 0–1M \'Fair\' band — the scheme\'s 4–5M \'Very good explanation\' rewards a developed description of a presentation strength (table easy to read; pictures add context).',
    source: 'LC Politics & Society 2025 OL marking scheme, Section B, Q3(b) ("Describe one positive about how the data is presented in Document B. 5 marks — Table is easy to read; Pictures add context; Very good explanation 4–5M")',
