    id: 'jceng-rewrite-punctuation-direct-speech-hl',
    subjectId: 'jc-english', subjectLabel: 'English (Junior Cycle)', level: 'higher',
    questionRef: '2023 HL · Section D · Q9',
    stem: 'Rewrite the following text, adding capital letters, commas, inverted commas, apostrophes and full stops correctly. You should create three lines of direct speech: tell me a story jane implored youre too old for stories her father sighed ill never be too old for stories jane insisted',
    commandWord: 'Rewrite',
    demand: 'Copy the passage out again with the mechanics fixed — this is a pure punctuation-accuracy task. Lay it out as three lines of direct speech, putting inverted commas around each spoken sentence, a capital to start each speaker\'s words, the apostrophes into \'you\'re\' and \'I\'ll\', and commas/full stops to close each quotation before the speech tag (implored / sighed / insisted).',
    trap: 'Marking is error-counting, not impression: every missing inverted comma, capital, apostrophe or full stop is a separate error. Forgetting the apostrophes in \'youre\'/\'ill\' or running the three speakers together instead of three laid-out lines piles up errors fast — 6-7 errors already drops you to 3 of 5, and 10+ errors scores 0. There is no reward for re-wording or \'improving\' the sentence — only for correct mechanics.',
    source: 'SEC JC English 2023 HL marking scheme, Section D, Q9 ("Candidates should demonstrate an understanding of the correct use of each of the punctuation marks"; banded by error count: 3 or fewer errors = 5, 10+ errors = 0)',
    marks: 5,
